            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nThis game helps you practice the connection between addition and multiplication—the idea that multiplying is just adding the same number many times (<htcite0>). If you haven't read the previous text yet, we recommend doing that first so the game makes more sense.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "eaa59295-fb80-4c33-b1e4-bcdf3c11dabf",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Adding the same numbers",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "5",
                        "day": "9"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_rules",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### How to Play\n\nYour mission is to strengthen your understanding of how addition and multiplication work together.\n\n**Step 1: Solve the addition.** You will see an addition problem on screen. Try to calculate the answer in your head first!\n\n**Step 2: Use the arrows.** When you are ready, use the side arrows (<i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-up upArrowWithFA\" style=\"font-size: 1.5em\"></i> <i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-down downArrowWithFA\" style=\"font-size: 1.5em\"></i>) to select the correct answer.\n\n**Step 3: Watch the image appear.** Each time you get a correct answer, the operation moves to the side and a new piece of an archaeological site or museum is revealed.\n\n**Step 4: Earn your medal!** When you complete all the calculations, you will receive a medal (<i class=\"fa-solid fa-medal\" style=\"color:gold;\"></i>). Click the arrow button (<i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i>) to try a new set of problems.\n\n**Tip:** The more you practice, the faster you will recognize the pattern between adding and multiplying!",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"htSequenceGame\"><div id=\"parentGame\" style=\"position: relative;\">  <img src=\"\" id=\"imgGame\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgGame', '0%')\" style=\"width: 60%;\" /><br /><span id=\"imgText\" style=\"display: inline-block; width: 250px; font-size: 0.8em\"></span> </div></p>",
